{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_work

    The whole of «Your work» in the app (local\yourwork), behind the home's «See all»: everything waiting to be sorted
    out, the urgent first; then each service, its door and, under it, its shortcuts. With nothing left (it was sorted out
    meanwhile), a line that says so.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * alertsheading, hasalerts, alerts (mobile_work_alert) - What is waiting.
    * servicesheading, doors (mobile_work_door, with hasactions and actions: label, url, browser) - The services.
    * hasdoors, none - Whether there is anything; the line for when there is not.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasdoors": false,
        "none": "Nada por resolver."
    }
}}
<div class="aty-home aty-trabajo">
    {{^hasdoors}}<p class="aty-trabajo-nada">{{none}}</p>{{/hasdoors}}
    {{#hasdoors}}
    {{#hasalerts}}
    <h2 class="aty-section">{{alertsheading}}</h2>
    <div class="aty-agenda">
        {{#alerts}}
        {{> local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_work_alert }}
        {{/alerts}}
    </div>
    {{/hasalerts}}
    <h2 class="aty-section">{{servicesheading}}</h2>
    <div class="aty-servicios">
        {{#doors}}
        <div class="aty-servicio">
            {{> local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_work_door }}
            {{#hasactions}}
            <div class="aty-atajos">
                {{#actions}}
                <a class="aty-atajo" core-link href="{{url}}" capture="{{^browser}}true{{/browser}}{{#browser}}false{{/browser}}"{{^browser}} inApp="true"{{/browser}}>{{label}}</a>
                {{/actions}}
            </div>
            {{/hasactions}}
        </div>
        {{/doors}}
    </div>
    {{/hasdoors}}
</div>
